We were driving from Liverpool to St Helens, and it was just dusk. From the car, above the road, we noticed a bright, orb-like light. Sometimes it would dim, then intensify significantly. It didn’t appear perfectly round but had star-like extensions coming out of it, pointing downward in two directions. The sky was cloudy, and it was clearly below the clouds. However, its distance was impossible to determine, but it was definitely flying much lower than helicopters. It didn’t change its position. We took several photos and videos. The attached photo was later zoomed in for better detail.
