This used to happen every night after sunset near us, but not usually this low. The pulsing ball of light hovers, and after some time (minutes in this case overall), it stops shining brightly, picks a direction and moves slowly with different, blinking lights.
These could be seen all over at the time, but this was extraordinarily low for point of view in the orb phase. While the "drone" mode or "patrol" mode is often quite low, the pulsing light / orb phase is usually not this low. It is unclear what exactly emits the lights in each phase, as we cannot see what is doing this - only the light. These are uniquely different than traditional orbs we've seen, such as ones able to rapidly accelerate. This pulsing, hovering, or slow moving ball of light was very common back in October - December 2024 in Connecticut, before New Jersey sightings gained media attention.
